      "guid": "com.maschine.raidmenucleanupfix",
      "name": "RaidMenuCleanupFix",
      "slug": "raidmenucleanupfix",
      "teaser": "Removes the brief freeze when opening the escape menu during a raid",
      "thumbnail": "https://forge-static.sp-tarkov.com/mods/BI4Ltp5mxo0cEXVJHQozOUYZH4OwuuYxAaEp4exK.png",
      "downloads": 4972,
      "favourites_count": 36,
      "description": "<h2>Overview</h2>\n<p>Did you ever accidentally hit Esc during a raid and got killed while you were staring and waiting for the Menu to open?<br />\nFor whatever reason BSG decided to run the post-raid cleanup not on post-raid (why would you?) but upon entering the Main Menu.</p>\n<p>This simple mod disables the cleanup process when opening the menu during a raid; afterwards, it runs as usual.<br />\nIt won’t affect performance, since you likely wouldn’t open the menu during a raid anyway.</p>\n<p>Not needed with Fika; if it is installed nonetheless, it simply does nothing.</p>\n<h2>Installation</h2>\n<p>As usual, unzip to SPT folder.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Let me know if you run into any problems or have suggestions for improvement.</p>\n",
      "detail_url": "https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/2733/raidmenucleanupfix",
      "fika_compatibility": true,
